{
    "word": "highborn",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "15e58eba-7d45-3558-b7a2-bff9f4e50bb5",
                "word": "highborn",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6fe1324c-e838-3416-9328-05fd689c36ca",
                        "entry_id": "15e58eba-7d45-3558-b7a2-bff9f4e50bb5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of high social standing as a result of having been born a member of an upper-level social class."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5733e836-829b-4d41-bdfe-2a246f47f861",
                                "sense_id": "6fe1324c-e838-3416-9328-05fd689c36ca",
                                "text": "I am too high-born to be propertied,\nTo be a secondary at control."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b31e522-b245-4b02-84be-d6508aba6e21",
                                "sense_id": "6fe1324c-e838-3416-9328-05fd689c36ca",
                                "text": "It is not for Kings to drink wine, nor for Princes strong drink. It becomes not them who are highborn to be intemperate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43edd232-200c-4e2c-95b1-7982a33fdb91",
                                "sense_id": "6fe1324c-e838-3416-9328-05fd689c36ca",
                                "text": "His acquaintance with this high-born dame gave wit no opportunity of boasting its influence; she was not to be subdued by the powers of verse, but rejected his addresses, it is said, with disdain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8713f46-7aab-491e-a48f-db8664ff2040",
                                "sense_id": "6fe1324c-e838-3416-9328-05fd689c36ca",
                                "text": "The young Irishman was not a little touched and elated by the high-born damsel's partiality for him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32e2cefe-2a6e-4bbd-9a70-18261c05d9f8",
                                "sense_id": "6fe1324c-e838-3416-9328-05fd689c36ca",
                                "text": "Was he not Rajah Hassim and was not the other a man of strong heart, of strong arm, of proud courage, a man great enough to protect highborn princes?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0592395-0f66-4895-8886-96b01e3b3e80",
                                "sense_id": "6fe1324c-e838-3416-9328-05fd689c36ca",
                                "text": "He is a career rather than a conviction politician, but too highborn to be written off as a mere scaler of the greasy pole. He is a scion of the class that, deep down, believes it was born to rule."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d14ce27-bfde-3d39-a160-f0f078454a82",
                        "entry_id": "15e58eba-7d45-3558-b7a2-bff9f4e50bb5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Born a member of an upper-level social class (although not necessarily retaining high social standing)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "06da5f9a-74a5-476a-885f-37b03e4c2fd9",
                                "sense_id": "9d14ce27-bfde-3d39-a160-f0f078454a82",
                                "text": "The selfish, base, covetous, father-in-law was not at all desirous to have a highborn beggar and the posterity of a highborn beggar to maintain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ae5e0c3-c439-4051-aed2-f1b07558d834",
                                "sense_id": "9d14ce27-bfde-3d39-a160-f0f078454a82",
                                "text": "The references to the lady's long-standing affection for her loyal, high-born servant girl provide a succinct intimation that the lady herself is not a wholly repellent character."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2f9e959-40c6-4037-b8e3-9436de114d63",
                                "sense_id": "9d14ce27-bfde-3d39-a160-f0f078454a82",
                                "text": "Mrs Monteith was able to tell her son about their high-born slave ancestor because he had left a memoir."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8457d415-0910-30de-aeec-07ac87ba607a",
                        "entry_id": "15e58eba-7d45-3558-b7a2-bff9f4e50bb5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, pertaining to, or befitting people of high social standing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0326a582-5a35-43ad-a52d-96cbecb1127f",
                                "sense_id": "8457d415-0910-30de-aeec-07ac87ba607a",
                                "text": "In this illustrious throng, your lofty flood\nSwells high, fair confluence of all highborn Blood."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a8cf3c2-d2c7-4e0c-84cd-258ce8550219",
                                "sense_id": "8457d415-0910-30de-aeec-07ac87ba607a",
                                "text": "I should have then\nBeen trained in no highborn necessities\nWhich I could meet not by my daily toil."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e18a5c3-fc80-4e07-aa0d-2c2cf44120fa",
                                "sense_id": "8457d415-0910-30de-aeec-07ac87ba607a",
                                "text": "Dowling says that most performances of Chekhov plays have been filtered through translations into a British highborn sensibility."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2b11a2c-4953-4a7b-bbdb-1486920da3a6",
                                "sense_id": "8457d415-0910-30de-aeec-07ac87ba607a",
                                "text": "If anyone in the highborn sport known as thoroughbred horse racing has swagger these days, it is Baffert."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "83d2e506-53c2-3fad-8523-a73efc480e2a",
                        "entry_id": "15e58eba-7d45-3558-b7a2-bff9f4e50bb5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of superior or premium quality; magnificent; expensive."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b8260e8-8fc3-405c-abd8-55f740dc2bb3",
                                "sense_id": "83d2e506-53c2-3fad-8523-a73efc480e2a",
                                "text": "The tires are highborn Pirelli P Zeroes in appropriately majestic sizes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bba0848-aab6-4b16-9c0a-c94b0aa91344",
                                "sense_id": "83d2e506-53c2-3fad-8523-a73efc480e2a",
                                "text": "Gearhart is worth taking a bit of time to ogle the highborn homes along the backroads near the beach."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8338ba01-a013-4da0-83e5-91c7d4475034",
                        "source_entry_id": "15e58eba-7d45-3558-b7a2-bff9f4e50bb5",
                        "source_sense_description": "of, pertaining to or befitting people of high social standing",
                        "target_lang_word": "urozený",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84ac0d17-d34e-4f64-99fc-1392244b2ed2",
                        "source_entry_id": "15e58eba-7d45-3558-b7a2-bff9f4e50bb5",
                        "source_sense_description": "of, pertaining to or befitting people of high social standing",
                        "target_lang_word": "bien né",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bien né",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fc3086a-610a-36ee-89b4-5e734a9941f9",
                                        "entry_id": "51044d3b-0e2b-3414-b35e-3921fb72a72c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui descend d’une famille noble."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d25f22d-2f71-49a2-b05b-acbd1a98e3e1",
                                                "sense_id": "3fc3086a-610a-36ee-89b4-5e734a9941f9",
                                                "text": "Il s’était obligé à se rendre à la grand-messe et à faire ses Pâques, parce qu’un homme bien né se doit de donner l’exemple, et que la religion est nécessaire au bon ordre de la société."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49753d51-3a2c-4703-95ac-1e3f1360d707",
                                                "sense_id": "3fc3086a-610a-36ee-89b4-5e734a9941f9",
                                                "text": "Sans cesse n’avait-elle pas à répondre à ses questions naïves sur mille choses simples qu’un enfant bien né n’ignore pas à quinze ans?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7bf2ef5-fed6-4909-8863-6e9270c2ed75",
                                                "sense_id": "3fc3086a-610a-36ee-89b4-5e734a9941f9",
                                                "text": "Ce roturier se haussait du col au point d'estimer qu'il avait, lui aussi, accès au suicide, cette marque de courage et de prestige réservée aux âmes bien nées !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2faf487-442d-3caf-99dc-84cee930c966",
                                        "entry_id": "51044d3b-0e2b-3414-b35e-3921fb72a72c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En parlant d'un cheval de course, dont les parents sont illustres ou qui a un pédigrée remarquable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Sports hippiques"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f976167-0699-46c5-98d7-bb39265e9b59",
                                                "sense_id": "a2faf487-442d-3caf-99dc-84cee930c966",
                                                "text": "Hélas, bien qu’extrêmement bien née, cette jument inédite n'eut pas une descendance à la hauteur de l’investissement, avec notamment de nombreux poulains ne parvenant pas à s’adapter aux méthodes d’entraînement américaines, d’où des problèmes de santé récurrents."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "262609b5-1cf2-4e18-aed9-529a49129261",
                                                "sense_id": "a2faf487-442d-3caf-99dc-84cee930c966",
                                                "text": "Le bien né Fabulous Wood débute par un succès."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
